% Powder Keg (resource scarcity: a spent reaction)
%
% A walled yard with one powder keg in it, sunk over an old cellar, and a
% tripwire across the yard. A bruiser stands guard by the keg; a lurker
% waits on the stair above. The team watches from the landing at the top
% of the stair. Nothing the team carries can stop either enemy - only the
% keg can: it blows the yard's floor into the cellar, and it blows once.
% Two companions, one skill each, from seven.
%
%   landing (team) --- stair (lurker) --- yard (keg, bruiser; tripwire)
%       |                                   |
%       +------------- side path --------- gate
%
% The keg is a telegraphed heavy attack the team sets off on purpose. Fire
% or a spark (burning, electrocuted) lights its fuse: it winds up a
% cave-in on the yard (the catalogue's caveIn, physical - it cannot be
% stopped). Then the yard's floor gives way and everything still in it
% falls into the cellar - the bruiser, the keg itself, and any companion
% who stayed. The keg is gone after that: it blows once.
%
% The tripwire is a plate: whatever is knocked onto it throws a spark
% into the powder trail, and the whole yard catches fire (spill(flames,
% yard)) - the keg with it.
%
% Methods (bring the lurker down into the yard, then light the keg):
%   gather   hook it down from the yard (the hooker then walks out), or
%            taunt it from the yard (it follows its taunter, so the
%            taunter has to stay - and goes down with the yard)
%   light    a fireball on the yard from the landing; a lightning flash
%            from the stair or the gate (its dash never lands in the new
%            chasm); a shield bash from the stair, or a vortex on the
%            tripwire from the landing, knocks the bruiser onto the
%            tripwire; a blinding flash in the yard (its caster is spent)
%
% Traps:
%   - lighting the keg first: the bruiser falls, the keg is spent, and
%     nobody can stand in the yard to bring the lurker down;
%   - a taunter who walks out of the yard takes the lurker with it;
%   - a tidal wave in the yard soaks the keg: the tripwire's fire only
%     makes steam.
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; every gatherer with every
% lighter wins (10 pairs), and no other pair does.

% === Map: four areas round a loop; the tripwire is a plate in the yard ===
region(landing).
region(stair).
region(yard).
region(gate).
connected(landing, stair).
connected(stair, yard).
connected(yard, gate).
connected(gate, landing).
lineOfSight(landing, yard).
lineOfSight(landing, stair).
lineOfSight(stair, yard).
lineOfSight(yard, stair).
lineOfSight(gate, yard).
lineOfSight(yard, gate).

feature(yard, tripwire, spark).
plate(tripwire).
effect(spark, target, spill(flames, yard)).

% === The keg: one fuse, one cave-in ===
role(keg, object).
at(keg, yard).
tag(keg, heavy).
behavior(keg, burning, caveIn, here).
behavior(keg, electrocuted, caveIn, here).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, landing).
at(mage, landing).
mana(player, 2).
mana(mage, 2).

% === Enemies ===
role(bruiser, enemy).
at(bruiser, yard).
tag(bruiser, living).

role(lurker, enemy).
at(lurker, stair).
tag(lurker, living).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, hook).
knows(mage, fireball).

% === Victory ===
% Bring the lurker into the yard; whoever stands in the yard walks out (or
% stays); then one cave-in takes both.
win :-
    if(),
    do(bringTo(lurker, yard, none), stepOut(), detonate(keg),
       confirmStopped(bruiser), confirmStopped(lurker)).

% Before the fuse is lit, the companions in the yard walk up to the
% landing - or stay, and go down with it (sacrifice is allowed). A taunted
% lurker follows its taunter out.
inYard(?a) :- canAct(?a), at(?a, yard), not(gone(?a)).
stepOut() :- if(not(first(inYard(?a)))), do().
stepOut() :- if(first(inYard(?a))), do(leaveYard()).
stepOut() :- if(first(inYard(?a))), do().
leaveYard() :- allOf, if(inYard(?a)), do(walkTo(?a, landing)).

% Light the keg: land the tag its fuse answers (fire, a spark), or knock
% something onto the tripwire.
detonate(?k) :-
    if(not(gone(?k)), behavior(?k, ?t, caveIn, here)),
    do(inflict(?t, ?k, none), confirmStopped(?k)).
detonate(?k) :-
    if(not(gone(?k)), at(?k, ?r), feature(?r, ?f, ?ab), plate(?f), at(?x, ?r), \==(?x, ?k)),
    do(knockOn(?x, feature(?f), none), confirmStopped(?k)).

funBlocker(bruiser).
funBlocker(lurker).
funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from seven (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(blindingFlash).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(5).

goals(win).
